once we got the eigenvalues of A are found, we can find all eigen vectors (the vectors that don’t change under the transformation) by solving (A-\lambda I)\vec{x}=\vec{0}

so on the diagonals you would remove \lambda and find the resulting matrix (like finding the linear combination for the zero vector)





