3: Discrete time signals
y[n] = \cos(n\pi/4) only exists at the integers n = -5, \dots, 5, so we used stem. The axis goes from -6 to 6 just so the plot isn’t cut off at the edges.
The period is N = \frac{2\pi}{\pi/4} = 8 samples, which is why y[0] = 1 and y[\pm 4] = -1.
